    "reason": "The alternating row `(10)^∞` is one of rule 30's three fixed points (Wolfram 1986 Table 6.2, crystals item 22). This is that fact in the only form the rest of the tier can use: a FINITE alternating stretch running left from the origin survives one step, one cell shorter at its left end, and -- this is the part that is not just 'it is a fixed point' -- the cell AT the origin survives regardless of what sits to the right of it, because the origin is black there and the `or` in `left XOR (centre OR right)` swallows the right neighbour. So a stretch that is alternating on positions `-(L+1)..0` is alternating on `-L..0` one step later, whatever the right half-line does. Each cell is one `rule30_eq` and a Bool case split; the only friction is that the three neighbours of `-(j)` are `-(j+1)`, `-(j)`, `-(j-1)`, so the index arithmetic crosses a ℕ-to-ℤ cast.",
